  "answer": "This has been requested before, both as a wider scrollbar and as an always-visible one. For always-visible, turn off Windows Settings > Accessibility (Ease of Access) > Display > 'Automatically hide scroll bars in Windows'. Terminal follows it, including in already-open windows, and the scrollbar stays visible. The wider scrollbar is harder: a width setting (terminal#9218) was discussed but not added. The maintainers have declined a Terminal-only width option (terminal#18937, closed), preferring to leave scrollbar sizing to Windows/WinUI rather than add per-app settings. Terminal#3454 tracks the always-visible request. You can add your accessibility need to that thread and to the WinUI repo, but there is currently no Terminal setting that widens the scrollbar."
